  "decisions": [
    "A broad historical retraining sweep is not justified. Only candidates with a direct ICL positive or near-positive endpoint and a conclusion-changing missing matched control were rerun.",
    "The adjusted 50/50 original-plus-ContextWorld data mixture is not the primary cause of the observed CEM losses: its matched-native effect is plus 3pp for Contact 4096 and minus 4pp with an interval crossing zero for Motion 2048.",
    "Exact conditional overlap is sufficient to create strong conditional ICL in the tested ActionDelay, Motion, and Contact recipes, but it is not sufficient to guarantee preservation of the ordinary planning function.",
    "Approximate Q/A matching adds a distinct nuisance-response failure in Contact; Motion shows that even exact Q/A overlap can conflict with planning when the learned response geometry does not transfer safely to planner-consumed queries.",
    "Future method attribution must report data-recipe, method, and deployment effects separately. Published-source success counts cannot be reused across evaluator processes as a causal baseline."
  ],
